; 05-local-extras-coalesce: ??'s code binds &1, &2 ... to its arguments past the first (a name bound in a call is a
; local one from then on: calls headed by it take their general way), whatever the first is.  (h ??) and (h 1 2)
; call through a local name (no plan learned, and h already bound), so (?? 1 2) is the first call of ?? with more
; than one argument.  The probe: (&1 v (g)) is Op2's (&1 is +) while &1 is no local's name, and the error made right
; after (zz is unbound) says where (g)'s code was ({+ 70000 70001}); once &1 is a local's name somewhere, (&1 v (g))
(def {&1} +)
(fun {g} {+ 70000 70001})
(fun {probe} {list (&1 v (g)) zz})
(fun {call2 h} {h 1 2})
(fun {test h} {do (map ?? {1 1 1}) (h ??)})
(test call2)
(def {v} 100003)
(probe)
(def {v} 100003)
(probe)
(def {v} 100003)
(probe)
